From 26811540dd23b382f0a80ab2f3011806f1f81b50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 07:05:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: flee excessive danger unless going after Morgoth

The 'Excessive danger' check in borg_caution() starts fleeing when the
danger at the borg's grid is more than twice its hit points, and its
comment says 'do not flee level if going after Morgoth or fighting a
unique'.  The condition required borg.ready_morgoth == 1, which is only
true once the borg is ready to face Morgoth, so in ordinary play the
check never fired and only the Morgoth-ready borg fled here.

Test ready_morgoth != 1, as the comment describes.  A badly hurt borg
in excessive danger now starts fleeing at once, which lets the following
escapes (such as the dash for a staircase a step or two away) apply to
it; a borg going after Morgoth no longer flees from this check.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#156.

(cherry picked from commit 007d45483832b2792ddde1b2c368b67975365496)
---
 src/borg/borg-caution.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-caution.c b/src/borg/borg-caution.c
index 313e3fe31..31aee65cd 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-caution.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-caution.c
@@ -1089,7 +1089,7 @@ bool borg_caution(void)
         /* do not flee level if going after Morgoth or fighting a unique */
         if (!borg.goal.fleeing && !borg.near.unique
             && (borg.trait[BI_CLEVEL] < 50) && !borg.status.vault
-            && (borg.trait[BI_CDEPTH] < 100 && borg.ready_morgoth == 1)) {
+            && (borg.trait[BI_CDEPTH] < 100 && borg.ready_morgoth != 1)) {
             /* Note */
             borg_note("# Fleeing (excessive danger)");
 
